{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC(b) IS NOW LIVE — the mcp_healthy alarm is applied and detecting\n\nOperator-approved apply completed. `aws cloudwatch describe-alarms` confirms:\n\n    rebar-mcp-serving-path-down | metric mcp_healthy | Statistic Minimum\n    Threshold 1.0 LessThanThreshold | period 300 | EP 3 | DTA 2\n    TreatMissingData breaching | 1 alarm action | State INSUFFICIENT_DATA (newly created)\n\nPlan was clean and minimal: **1 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy** — this creates a new alarm and touches no existing paging behaviour.\n\n## A false-page risk I checked BEFORE calling this done\n\nThe alarm is `treat_missing_data = breaching`, so if the probe that publishes `mcp_healthy` were not yet running on the host, the alarm would have gone to ALARM within ~15 minutes and paged for a non-problem. Verified it will not:\n\n- `get-metric-statistics` returns **22 mcp_healthy datapoints in the last 2 hours** — the metric is publishing.\n- The probe is deployed: `grep -c mcp_healthy /opt/rebar/infra/scripts/observability.sh` = 3, file dated Sep 3 07:33.\n- `systemctl is-active rebar-observability.timer` = **active**.\n\nSo INSUFFICIENT_DATA is simply a newly-created alarm awaiting its first evaluation periods, not a missing publisher.\n\n## What had to be fixed first, and why it matters\n\nChange 2565 landed this alarm with a **1236-raw / 1180-dedented character** `alarm_description` against AWS's 1024 cap, so it was **unappliable** — `terraform plan` errored outright. That reached main through LLM-Review and a green Verified vote because nothing in the pipeline plans against AWS: `terraform validate` parses HCL and passes, the alarm guards checked structure rather than provider constraints, and CI never runs a plan. It surfaced only when an operator asked for the apply.\n\nChange 2584 trimmed the description to 775 characters and added `test_alarm_descriptions_fit_the_aws_limit`, which now covers BOTH the heredoc and quoted-string spellings (monitoring.tf uses the quoted form three times, so a heredoc-only guard would have skipped exactly those) and carries an anti-vacuity floor of 15 measured descriptions. It measures what terraform actually sends — `<<-` strips the common indent, and counting raw would have failed the valid, live `bedrock_invoke_client_errors` at 1037 when AWS reports its description as 982.\n\n## Where this ticket stands\n\n- AC(b) — unhealthy upstream detected and reported: **DONE and LIVE**. Nothing could observe a /mcp outage for the 12 hours of this incident; that gap is now closed in production.\n- AC(c) — regression test / operational probe: **DONE** (change 2565's shell tests, RED-proven).\n- AC(a) — prevent the OOM: measurement-only instrumentation is in flight per the operator's decision. No memory limit or instance size will be chosen until there are numbers, because today every candidate value is a guess.\n\nEndpoint is healthy: `/mcp` returns 401 (auth required), not 502."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788463226481896001,"uuid":"e3bc209a-54c4-4299-9ea3-21a2cdbefeb5"}